#!args scenario=Scenario_Debug_USA seed=42
#
# Rosie the Riveter runs BEFORE the discard step, and its cards go to the BOTTOM of the draw deck.
#
# "Use once per turn at the beginning of your Discard step. Take 1 or 2 cards from your hand and
# place them on the bottom of your draw deck." The card used to declare a plain
# IsGameFlowStep(DISCARD) trigger, which is not a reaction window and so was never a chance to use
# it: GameFlow.BeginStep runs the BEFORE mutators and then hands straight to the discard handler,
# whose DiscardHandCardsChangeEvent carries IsTrigger = false. It is now a BEFORE-DISCARD
# IStepMutator on the card logic itself, registered by DeckState.PlayCard with the Status card.
#
# Scenario_Debug_USA opens on the US with Rosie already on the table and openingDiscard off, so turn
# 1 IS the US turn and no opening discards stand in the way.
#
# The four things pinned below:
#
#   1. ORDER      the Rosie prompt arrives before the discard prompt, not after it.
#   2. BOTTOM     the picks land at the bottom of the deck, in the order chosen.
#   3. NO DISCARD they never pass through the discard pile on the way (the old version applied a
#                 DiscardHandCardsChangeEvent first, filing them as discarded this turn).
#   4. SCOPED     only the owner's own Discard step — Germany's next turn gets no Rosie prompt.
#
# Card ids are pinned to the seed in the #!args line: 186 (Build Navy) and 180 (Build Army) are in
# the US opening hand at that seed. Re-derive them after any change to the shuffle.
#
# Run:  tests/run-cli.sh tests/qgc/rosie_before_discard.qgc

prompt                                  # turn 1, US, PLAY_CARD — synchronise with the running game

assert faction == UNITED_STATES
assert step == PLAY_CARD
assert card StatusRosietheRiveter in status
assert handsize UNITED_STATES == 7
assert decksize UNITED_STATES == 25

pass                                    # no play this turn; walk on to the discard step

# (1) ORDER. This prompt is Rosie's, raised by the mutator before the discard handler starts. It is
# the discard prompt instead ("choose up to 7") if the mutator did not run.
prompt
assert step == DISCARD
assert promptoptions == 7                # the whole hand is offered, capped at 2 picks

answer id=186,180                        # Build Navy first, then Build Army

# The normal discard step follows, as it would with no Rosie in play at all — and it is the SECOND
# prompt of this step, not the first. Its option count is the hand Rosie left behind: 5, not 7.
prompt
assert promptfaction == UNITED_STATES
assert promptoptions == 5

# (2) BOTTOM, in the order chosen: 186 then 180, so 180 is last.
assert handsize UNITED_STATES == 5
assert decksize UNITED_STATES == 27
assert deckbottom UNITED_STATES == 180
assert card 186 in deck

# (3) NO DISCARD — nothing has reached the discard pile, these two least of all.
assert discardsize UNITED_STATES == 0

pass                                     # under the hand cap, so declining the discard is legal

# (4) SCOPED to the owner. The draw step refills the US hand from the TOP, so both recycled cards
# must still be in the deck afterwards — they would be straight back in hand had they gone to the
# top. And this prompt is Germany's own turn, not a second Rosie window.
prompt
assert faction == GERMANY
assert card 186 in deck
assert card 180 in deck
assert handsize UNITED_STATES == 7

quit
